  "name": "html-empty-table-cell-reserves-width",
  "description": "An empty `display:table-cell` that declares a width still takes that share of its table row. The three-cell header reserves 25% for an empty trailing cell; dropping it handed the share to its siblings, so the centred menu cell moved from x=380 w=680 to x=493 w=907 at 1440px. The empty cell survives as an empty group carrying its source class, so the author's table rule keeps sizing it.",
